course: dictionary
lesson: 15116
title: Saline: salty water
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Saline is a word for salt. If something is saline, it contains salt, so it tastes salty. Look at the words around it to be sure. «Seawater is saline, so it tastes very salty.» The sea is full of salt, so saline must mean salty.
explain: In hospital, saline means clean salty water. «The nurse rinsed the cut with saline.» Nurses use it to wash wounds and rinse eyes, and it can go into a drip. When saline is a noun, it is the salt water itself: you can say «a bag of saline».
explain: Here is a quick check. Swap in the word salty and read the sentence again: «Seawater is salty» still makes sense. Context tells you the meaning, and the dictionary confirms it.
fact: Saline means containing salt or salty.
fact: Seawater is saline. River water is usually fresh, which means it is not salty.
fact: Saline (noun), or saline solution, is clean salty water used in medicine.
fact: Nurses and doctors use saline to wash wounds, rinse eyes and contact lenses, and in a drip.
fact: A saline lake is a lake with a lot of salt in its water.
exercise: «Seawater is saline, so you should not drink it.» What does saline mean? | *Salty | Cold as ice | Fresh and clean from a river | Sweet like sugar
exercise: «The nurse rinsed the cut with saline.» In this sentence, what is saline? | A small pill to swallow | A kind of bandage | A type of soap | *Clean salty water used in medicine
exercise: Find and copy the one word in «Seawater is saline, but river water is fresh» that means the opposite of saline. | seawater | water | river | *fresh
test: «The doctor put a saline drip in her arm.» What is the saline here? | A kind of medicine pill | Cold air | A bandage | *Salty water used in hospital
test: Which place is most likely to have saline water? | A river of fresh rainwater | *The sea | A bottle of lemonade | A snowy mountain top
exam: Which of these is the best way to describe seawater? | Brown and muddy | Sweet and sugary | *Saline, containing lots of salt | Warm and fresh
